     "text": "{\"events\": [{\"detail\": \"Built on the foundations of the Goevrouwetoren (Goede Vrouwtoren / Go\u00ea Vrouwentoren) by Adriaan de Booys; permission granted in 1778, officially opened 19 May 1779.\", \"event\": \"built\", \"year\": 1779}, {\"detail\": \"A steam engine was placed in the windmill, transformed into a wind and steam mill to grind corn; not a commercial success.\", \"event\": \"extended\", \"year\": 1865}, {\"detail\": \"Severely damaged by a storm; grinding flour continued until then.\", \"event\": \"damaged\", \"year\": 1930}, {\"detail\": \"On the evening of 23 April 1932 the windmill burnt down completely; fire brigade could not prevent complete burning; extinguishing lasted for days; cause never established.\", \"event\": \"burnt\", \"year\": 1932}, {\"detail\": \"Rebuilding on the original foundations started; first pole / stone put in the ground 21 April 1999.\", \"event\": \"rebuilt\", \"year\": 1999}, {\"detail\": \"Rebuilt windmill reopened 23 April 2002, exactly 70 years after the fire.\", \"event\": \"rebuilt\", \"year\": 2002}], \"sources\": [\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Adriaan,_Haarlem\", \"https://www.molenadriaan.nl/en/timeline/\"]}",
